Package: exmort
Title: All-Cause and Excess Mortality Calculator
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shanlong", "Ding", email = "dings@who.int",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("World Health Organization Regional Office for the Western Pacific",
           role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: An interactive 'shiny' application that estimates all-cause
    mortality and excess mortality from country-level weekly or monthly death
    counts. Users supply observed deaths and an event calendar (for example
    COVID-19 waves or typhoons); the app fits one or more statistical
    baseline models (historical average, negative binomial regression,
    quasi-Poisson regression, zero-inflated Poisson regression, ARIMA
    (autoregressive integrated moving average) and SARIMA (seasonal ARIMA)
    models, GAM (generalized additive model) splines, and the model of
    Karlinsky and Kobak (2021) <doi:10.7554/eLife.69336>) on a user-defined
    baseline period, projects the expected deaths into the post-baseline
    period, and reports excess deaths, P-scores (excess deaths as a
    percentage of expected deaths) and confidence limits with tables, plots
    and downloadable reports. Launch the application with run_app().
